#: contents/ui/configGeneral.qml:1232
msgid "Drag the floating Notch along the edge (or use the arrow keys; Home centers it); the position is remembered for each edge. Wayland (KDE Plasma): uses the layer-shell protocol, so panels appearing or disappearing never move it. X11: a plain always-on-top window without reserved area. If the layer-shell QML module is missing the option has no effect and the Notch stays in the panel; other compositors without layer-shell may show a regular window. Only for a widget in a panel (not on the desktop). With a specific screen, only the widget in a panel of that screen floats; two widgets on the same screen overlap, so enable it in one. Right-click the floating Notch for Configure."
msgstr "Drag the floating Notch along the edge (or use the arrow keys; Home centers it); the position is remembered for each edge. Wayland (KDE Plasma): uses the layer-shell protocol, so panels appearing or disappearing never move it. X11: a plain always-on-top window without reserved area. If the layer-shell QML module is missing the option has no effect and the Notch stays in the panel; other compositors without layer-shell may show a regular window. Only for a widget in a panel (not on the desktop). With a specific screen, only the widget in a panel of that screen floats; two widgets on the same screen overlap, so enable it in one. Right-click the floating Notch for Configure."

